# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sentinel-infra — environment (Terraform)
# Copy to the Sentinel-infra repo as `.env` (gitignored). Values here drive
# `terraform` locally; in CI the same values are GitHub *variables* (+ one
# secret) per infra §9, and Azure auth is OIDC (no client secret).
# Reconstructed from architecture/infra.md §4, §5, §8, §9, §10.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Azure identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# rev-9 (2026-08-15): the CI identity is the `sentinel-gha` USER-ASSIGNED MANAGED
# IDENTITY, not an app registration. The subscription lives in the uwindsor.ca
# tenant where we hold no directory rights. See infra.md §4.2.
AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=174e25ca-ab82-4671-a913-9c2f66e5924d
AZURE_TENANT_ID=12f933b3-3d61-4b19-9a4d-689021de8cc9
AZURE_CLIENT_ID=                    # az identity show -n sentinel-gha -g sentinel-rg --query clientId -o tsv
#                                     ^ clientId, NOT principalId
# For LOCAL `terraform apply` just `az login` interactively and omit the ARM_* trio.
# For non-interactive local runs (and in CI, where OIDC supplies the token):
# ARM_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=${AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID}
# ARM_TENANT_ID=${AZURE_TENANT_ID}
# ARM_CLIENT_ID=${AZURE_CLIENT_ID}
# ARM_USE_OIDC=true

# ── Terraform input variables (variables.tf → TF_VAR_*) ────────────────────────
# R3 RESOLVED 2026-08-15 → canadacentral. Note `var.location` has NO default in HCL
# on purpose; it is supplied here locally and via the AZURE_LOCATION GitHub variable
# in CI (C5). Still to confirm on a live subscription: BASv2 vCPU quota >= 2 for the
# AKS B2ats_v2 node, and F1 App Service availability.
TF_VAR_location=canadacentral
TF_VAR_subscription_id=${AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID}
TF_VAR_resource_group_name=sentinel-rg
# rev-9: NO TF_VAR_postgres_entra_admin_group_object_id. The sentinel-db-admins group
# is gone (creating a group is a directory write we cannot perform); Postgres Entra
# admins are attached directly — you, plus the backend UAMI. infra.md §3.2.
TF_VAR_postgres_entra_admin_object_id=      # az ad signed-in-user show --query id -o tsv
TF_VAR_postgres_entra_admin_principal_name= # az ad signed-in-user show --query userPrincipalName -o tsv
# rev-5: NO TF_VAR_db_password. Postgres is Entra-only (password_auth_enabled=false).
TF_VAR_github_owner=Keshav0375      # real owner (case-sensitive — OIDC `sub` must match exactly)
TF_VAR_github_pat=                  # GitHub PAT, `repo` scope. In CI this is the GH_PAT
#                                     secret — NOT `GITHUB_PAT`; GitHub reserves that
#                                     prefix and rejects the name outright (C6).

# ── Remote state backend (bootstrapped manually once, infra §8.1) ──────────────
# These match backend.tf; the storage account must already exist. Auth is Entra
# (use_azuread_auth), which is why the CI identity needs Storage Blob Data
# Contributor on the account — it sits outside the sentinel-rg Contributor scope (C2).
TF_STATE_RESOURCE_GROUP=sentinel-state-rg
TF_STATE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT=sentineltfstate
TF_STATE_CONTAINER=tfstate
TF_STATE_KEY=sentinel.terraform.tfstate

# ── Runtime secrets to load into Key Vault AFTER apply (infra §10 step 7) ───────
# Not Terraform inputs — set via `az keyvault secret set`. Listed here so you can
# collect them in one place before the bootstrap. 9 secrets:
# anthropic-api-key ↻, openai-api-key ↻, dd-api-key, dd-app-key, teams-webhook-url,
# langfuse-secret-key, langfuse-public-key, acr-password, github-pat
# ↻ = seeded with a ~90d expiry; rotated by the rotator Function (infra §3.8, task 3.6).
# rev-5 REMOVED: db-password (Entra-only Postgres), sentinel-api-token (Entra bearer auth).
